/*
  Delta.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0081 · Delta (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web `<Delta>`
  (components/data-display/Delta.tsx) renders only two pieces of user-facing copy — both VoiceOver /
  tooltip `title` strings — which resolve here through the same `t()` keys the web uses, mirrored so
  the native reproduction holds no hardcoded prose:

    • delta.title         — the populated indicator's spoken title (web
                            `t('delta.title', '{{current}} vs {{previous}}')`). `%1$@` / `%2$@` are
                            the formatted endpoints, positional so a translation may reorder them.
    • delta.noComparison  — the empty / loading indicator's label (web
                            `t('delta.noComparison', 'No comparison data')`).

  The visible value text ("↑ 4.7%", "$3.50", "14.0 mi (4.7%)", "—") and the caller-supplied
  `comparedTo` ("vs last week") are composed from glyphs + locale-formatted numbers + caller strings;
  the web does not translate them either, so they carry no keys here.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are
  kept in a per-surface table ("Delta") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings.
*/

/* --- VoiceOver / tooltip titles (web Delta `t()`) --- */
"delta.title" = "%1$@ vs %2$@";
"delta.noComparison" = "No comparison data";
